Simon,

I have added a high-level method "createRJavaRef" to JRI 0.3-7. It  
also supports raw REXP assigns, so you can do something like:

re.assign("o", re.createRJavaRef(o));

You can get the most recent development version of rJava (which  
includes JRI) from
http://rforge.net/rJava/

Cheers,
Simon

