Sun's Java before 1.6.0 beta 2 on 64-bit Linux had a serious bug that  
prevented it from running via JNI. That has been fixed and iPlots/JGR  
is known to work with Sun's Java 1.6.0 on 64-bit Linux (tested on  
Debian) without problems. There were reports that FC's packaged RPM  
doesn't work, but if installed from Sun's files, it does. We don't  
have a FC system, so I'm only relaying information received.

Cheers,
Simon

