> I notice that it writes foo.jpg to /tmp/Rserve/conn129. I imagine  
> that each different Rconnection has its own directory under /tmp/ 
> Rserve.
>
> Given an Rconnection object, is there a way I can find out what its  
> own temp directory is?

Yes:

conn.eval("getwd()").asString()

FWIW: unless you have a special application you should consider using  
Rserve's I/O API which doesn't require you to specify full path and  
works even with remote Rserve, so you can retrieve the above file with

RFileInputStream fis = conn.openFile("foo.jpg");
...

For a full example that creates a plot, reads it through R's I/O and  
displays it on screen see PlotDemo.java in the examples directory.

Cheers,
Simon

