> 
> this actually the standard behavior in a unix shell, so you shouldn't be 
> surprised ;). When you start a process from the shell in the background, 
> the shell will still send HUP to it when it closes and it will wait for 
> its children to close. This is why the shell appears to hang and yet 
> Rserve gets closed. It is advisable to use `nohup' if you want to run it 
> from a shell and be able to close the shell without shutting down Rserve.
> In a sense I understand your confusion, because some other daemons use 
> HUP for other purposes (e.g. reloading configuration), but Rserve doesn't.
