You didn't set DISPLAY so can't use jpeg(..), this is your problem  
number one. The "Execution halted" comes from the R child that was  
connected to your client and it correctly quits. This has nothing to  
do with the Rserve itself, because that is another, separate process  
(save for debug mode).


> ...and then of course my application fails from that point. (BTW,  
> even though it says "execution halted", ps still reports an Rserve  
> process).

Why "of course"? Can you elaborate on that? The above error doesn't  
affect Rserve, so can you be more specific as of what fails? The  
above also doesn't have anything to do with a shell, so I'm wondering  
what you are really asking here ;) ...

In fact even w/o nohup it works fine for me on Linux:

caladan:urbanek$ ssh co
urbanek@corrino:~$ R CMD Rserve
[...]
Rserv started in daemon mode.
urbanek@corrino:~$ exit
logout

caladan:urbanek$ ssh co
urbanek@corrino:~$ ps ax|grep [R]se
28357 ?        Ss     0:00 /usr/lib/R/bin/Rserve
urbanek@corrino:~$ R
[...]
 > library(Rserve)
 > c=RSconnect()
 > RSeval(c,"'hello, world'")
[1] "hello, world"

Note that at this point there are two separate Rserve processes:
urbanek@corrino:~$ ps ax|grep [R]se
28357 ?        Ss     0:00 /usr/lib/R/bin/Rserve
28578 ?        S      0:00 /usr/lib/R/bin/Rserve

the original server process and a client process. The latter will go  
away when you nuke it or close the connection.

Cheers,
Simon


