Can you send me the full transcript, please? Also please send me the  
output of
sudo R CMD sh -c 'echo $PATH;echo $R_HOME; which Rserve'

My guess would be that you have an old version of Rserve somewhere on  
your PATH for one reason or another ...

> Also, I do not have a command called Xvfb on my machine. Is there  
> another command I can use?
>

Xvfb is X11 server using virtual frame buffer, so it is a kind of  
'headless' X11 server. You can usually find it in /usr/X11R6/bin, but  
if you don't have it, then you are in trouble, because you 'll need  
to think of another solution. In fact I don't recommend using jpeg 
(..) precisely because it's a mess, slow and the output is not very  
good anyway - you may consider using GDD or Cairo instead - those  
don't need a running X11 server and have better rendering.

Cheers,
Simon


