Message-ID: <45B696C2.2010807@systemsbiology.org>

I solved this.

Here's how I did it...when I built gd it put its libraries in 
/usr/local/libs. It seemed that GDD was looking for them in 
/usr/lib64/libgd, so I copied the libs in /usr/local/libs there (first 
backing up some older ones in /usr/lib64/libgd that probably did not 
support that missing function). I rebuilt GDD to be safe (not sure if 
that step was necessary) and then the library(GDD) command worked, and I 
could create plots, etc.



