> following error-message is thrown:
>
>   [sshexec]
> java.library.path=/opt/sun-jdk-1.5.0.09/jre/lib/i386/server:/opt/ 
> sun-jdk-1.5.0.09/jre/lib/i386:/opt/sun-jdk-1.5.0.09/jre/../lib/ 
> i386:/home/jsc/r/src/R-2.4.1/bin:/home/jsc/r/src/R-2.4.1/lib:/home/ 
> jsc/r/src/JRI
>   [sshexec] Cannot find JRI native library!
>   [sshexec] Please make sure that the JRI native library is in a
> directory listed in java.library.path.
>   [sshexec] java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError:
> /home/jsc/r/src/JRI/libjri.so: /home/jsc/r/src/JRI/libjri.so:
> undefined symbol: R_CStackLimit
>
> I think the root of the problem in libjri.so is to be found in
> ./src/Rinit.c where R_CStackLimit is maybe not properly initialised. I
> didn't find any hints on the problem. Does anyone of you know
> solutions to this or had the same problem?
>

Please make sure you have the correct R version, or rather that there  
is not an old R version lurking around. R_CStackLimit is defined in R  
2.3.1 and higher, but was not in previous versions. If you pick up an  
older R version for one reason or another, it would fail exactly as  
above.

Please review the settings in the run script, in particular  
LD_LIBRARY_PATH.

If you still have problems, please tell us precisely what rJava/JRI  
version you are using, more information on the unix system (type,  
version, hardware) and the full run script.

Thanks,
